.TH PDP-AGENT-INSTALL 8 "" "pdp-agent" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
pdp-agent-install \- configure, enrol and start the PDP endpoint agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pdp-agent-install
.B \-\-server
.I URL
.B \-\-ca\-sha256
.I FINGERPRINT
.RB [ \-\-token
.IR TOKEN ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes
.I /etc/pdp/agent.json
and
.I /etc/pdp/agent.env
(mode 0600: enrolment token, CA fingerprint and agent image reference), optionally loads
.RB ( \-\-image\-tar )
or pulls
.RB ( \-\-pull )
the agent container image, compares the fingerprint with the server's
.I /dl/ca.pem
and then enables and starts
.BR pdp-agent.service ,
which runs the agent image with docker.
The agent enrols on first start with the one-time token; later starts reuse the identity in
.IR /var/lib/pdp .
.SH OPTIONS
Run
.B pdp-agent-install \-\-help
for the full list:
.BR \-\-agent\-url ,
.BR \-\-image ,
.BR \-\-image\-tar ,
.BR \-\-pull ,
.BR \-\-source ,
.BR \-\-tz ,
.BR \-\-no\-verify ,
.BR \-\-no\-start ,
.BR \-\-force .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/pdp-agent.service
the service unit
.TP
.I /usr/share/pdp-agent/
example configuration files
.TP
.I /var/lib/pdp/
agent identity, spool and detection bundles (kept on package removal)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR docker (1)
